.TH mp3x 1 "July 27, 2026" "LAME 4.1" "LAME audio compressor"
.SH NAME
mp3x \- frame analyzer for the LAME mp3 encoder
.SH SYNOPSIS
mp3x [options] [infile]
.SH DESCRIPTION
mp3x encodes an audio file one mp3 frame at a time and shows what the encoder
did with each frame: the input waveform, the frequency spectrum it quantizes,
what the psychoacoustic model decided to mask, and how closely the decoded
result matches the input.
It is a tool for understanding an encode, not for producing one \- no mp3 file
is written.
.PP
Input may be WAV, AIFF or mp3, or standard input if
.B \-
is given.
An mp3 input is decoded and re\-encoded, which is what lets the analyzer show
both sides of the comparison.
.PP
Any
.BR lame (1)
option given on the command line applies to that first file, so the effect of a
particular encoder setting can be watched directly.
Files opened later from the File menu use LAME's normal defaults instead; the
initial command line is not replayed.
.PP
mp3x is not built by default.
It is available when LAME was configured with
.B \-\-enable\-mp3x
and the system provides GTK 4.10 or newer and libmpg123 1.26 or newer with
decoder support enabled.
.SH THE GRAPHS
Eight graphs are shown.
Where a graph is per\-granule there are two, one for each granule of the frame;
which channel is drawn is chosen with the display controls below.
.TP
.B PCM
The input audio of the current frame.
.TP
.B Re\-synthesis
The original input and the encode\-then\-decode result drawn on top of each
other \- the direct picture of what the encoder discarded.
It can also draw the difference between them instead of the overlay, which
makes small deviations legible.
.TP
.B MDCT spectrum
The log energy of the 576 MDCT lines, which is the frequency\-domain
representation the encoder actually quantizes.
Scalefactor\-band boundaries are marked over it by default.
.TP
.B Psychoacoustics
Per scalefactor band: the signal energy as bars, with the masking threshold and
the actual quantization noise as lines.
Where the noise line lies below the threshold line the model expects the noise
to be inaudible; where it rises above, it does not.
.TP
.B Scalefactors
The scalefactor magnitude chosen for each band, as upright bars.
Long and short blocks are laid out differently: a short block shows its bands
across the three windows.
.SH DISPLAY CONTROLS
These change what the graphs draw and take effect on the next redraw.
.TP
.B Channel
Left or right.
.TP
.B M/S
Switch the channel selector from left/right to mid/side, for frames the encoder
coded as joint stereo.
.TP
.B Difference
Make the re\-synthesis graph draw decoded minus original rather than the two
overlaid.
.TP
.B Source
Read the MDCT and scalefactor graphs from the LAME encoder side or from the
mpg123\-decoded side.
For an mp3 input the two can differ, and that difference is often the
interesting part.
.TP
.B Scalefactor\-band lines
The band boundaries drawn over the MDCT spectrum.
On by default.
.TP
.B Spectrum axis
Plot the psychoacoustic graph with one point per scalefactor band, which is the
default and what the noise comparison needs, or one point per FFT bin for a
finer view.
.TP
.B Subblock
For a short block, which of the three interleaved windows to draw.
All three are shown by default.
.SH KEYBOARD
.TP
.B Space
Play or pause the analysis.
.TP
.B Right arrow
Step forward one frame.
.TP
.B Left arrow
Step back one frame.
.TP
.B 1, 2, 3
Show only that subblock window.
.TP
.B 0
Show all three subblock windows.
.TP
.B Ctrl+O
Open a file.
.TP
.B Ctrl+W
Close the current file.
.TP
.B Ctrl+S
Save a screenshot.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Q
Quit.
.PP
On macOS the Command key replaces Ctrl for the last four.
.SH STATISTICS
The statistics view accumulates over every frame analyzed so far, not only the
one on screen: how many frames have been analyzed, the mean and maximum
main\-data bits per frame, the bits a frame can hold at this bitrate, and counts
of the frames or granules that used de\-emphasis, mid/side stereo, intensity
stereo, short blocks, mixed blocks and preflag.
Those counts are a quick way to see which encoder decisions a piece of audio is
actually provoking.
.SH SAVING
Each graph can be saved as a PNG on its own, and a composite renders all eight
into a single image laid out like the on\-screen stack.
The composite is re\-rendered at a fixed size rather than captured from the
window, so it does not vary with how the window happens to be sized.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lame (1)
